OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSACampaign to ditch town's
OL,4,A'erroneous' hyphens
OL,5,
OL,6,FNow the town council and local
OL,7,Fbusinesses have launched a campaign to
OL,8,Fclaim back their name and are calling
OL,9,Fon Tripadvisor, Wikipedia and GWR to
OL,10,Falso support them.
OL,12,FTom Vaughton, founder and CEO of Varn
OL,13,FSearch Marketing, began the campaign
OL,14,Fafter spotting there were 5,800
OL,15,F"erroneous hyphens" appearing online.
